{
  "version": 1,
  "comments": {
    "c1": {
      "anchor": "i53",
      "kind": "item",
      "label": "The read through says a yes or no field is never filled when every row says no",
      "excerpt": "The read through says a yes or no field is never filled when every row says no",
      "text": "details",
      "by": "owenoak",
      "at": "2026-11-04T11:54:27.668Z",
      "status": "answered",
      "replies": [
        {
          "by": "owenoak",
          "agent": "claude",
          "at": "2026-11-04T12:06:23.459Z",
          "html": "<p>Found it: \"never filled\" compares each value with a new thing's, so a yes/no that's no on every row looks unsent. Recommended (A): filled means a row stored a value there, which the engine already tracks; about 5 lines and a test. Details in the item, I53.</p>"
        }
      ],
      "claim": {
        "by": "owenoak",
        "agent": "claude",
        "at": "2026-11-04T11:59:02.181Z"
      }
    },
    "c2": {
      "anchor": "i60",
      "kind": "item",
      "label": "spellml's <comment> is a comment: Spell UI's ui-comment draws only as <ui-comment>",
      "excerpt": "spellml's <comment> is a comment: Spell UI's ui-comment draws only as <ui-comment>",
      "text": "details",
      "by": "owenoak",
      "at": "2026-11-04T11:55:30.513Z",
      "status": "answered",
      "replies": [
        {
          "by": "owenoak",
          "agent": "claude",
          "at": "2026-11-04T12:06:24.117Z",
          "html": "<p>Found it: in a drawing, spellml's own tag words win over components' short names, and <code>comment</code> is one, so everything up to <code>&lt;/comment&gt;</code> is its text. Recommended (A): a message when a comment in a drawing holds markup, naming <code>&lt;ui-comment&gt;</code>; about 10 lines. Details in the item, I60.</p>"
        }
      ],
      "claim": {
        "by": "owenoak",
        "agent": "claude",
        "at": "2026-11-04T11:59:03.016Z"
      }
    },
    "c3": {
      "anchor": "i61",
      "kind": "item",
      "label": "A property named like a saved collection quietly takes its adds",
      "excerpt": "A property named like a saved collection quietly takes its adds",
      "text": "details",
      "by": "owenoak",
      "at": "2026-11-04T11:56:11.240Z",
      "status": "answered",
      "replies": [
        {
          "by": "owenoak",
          "agent": "claude",
          "at": "2026-11-04T12:06:24.779Z",
          "html": "<p>Found it: <code>the todos</code> means the property when there is one, and adding to a property's read is a plain append, never a save. Recommended (A): warn on any add or remove whose list is a read of saved things, which catches <code>its own todos</code> too; about 15 lines. Details in the item, I61.</p>"
        }
      ],
      "claim": {
        "by": "owenoak",
        "agent": "claude",
        "at": "2026-11-04T11:59:03.793Z"
      }
    },
    "c4": {
      "anchor": "i54",
      "kind": "item",
      "label": "Looking again keeps the notes of the look before, stale ones too",
      "excerpt": "Looking again keeps the notes of the look before, stale ones too",
      "text": "details",
      "by": "owenoak",
      "at": "2026-11-04T11:56:38.383Z",
      "status": "answered",
      "replies": [
        {
          "by": "owenoak",
          "agent": "claude",
          "at": "2026-11-04T12:06:25.459Z",
          "html": "<p>Found it: a same-shape update keeps every old note, so the agent's advice isn't lost, but every check's note sticks too. Recommended (A): keep the agent's notes in their own list, and let each look say the rest afresh; about 25 lines and a test. Details in the item, I54.</p>"
        }
      ],
      "claim": {
        "by": "owenoak",
        "agent": "claude",
        "at": "2026-11-04T11:59:04.535Z"
      }
    }
  },
  "on": {}
}
